docs/adr/0019-batch-pull-request-self-target-readiness.md:3:When automatic Batch Pull Request creation is enabled, Symphony opens one pull request from the Loop-Start Branch to the configured Pull Request Base Branch. GitHub rejects a pull request whose head and base are the same branch, and letting that fail at handoff time leaves completed work with a retryable-looking error that operator action cannot fix by retrying.
docs/adr/0019-batch-pull-request-self-target-readiness.md:7:This preserves the existing Batch Pull Request model and avoids attempting impossible PR handoffs after task work has already completed.
docs/adr/0016-issue-comments-in-agent-context.md:1:# ADR 0016: Issue Comments in Agent Context
docs/adr/0016-issue-comments-in-agent-context.md:7:Prompts include those comments when present, and Stage Goal Context carries the same comment data
docs/adr/0016-issue-comments-in-agent-context.md:8:when Stage Goal Handoff is enabled.
docs/adr/0016-issue-comments-in-agent-context.md:10:Issue comments supplement the Agent Prompt and Stage Goal Context. They do not replace the issue
docs/adr/0020-task-pull-request-mode.md:5:The Pull Request Policy now includes `mode`, defaulting to `batch`. In `batch` mode, Symphony preserves existing Batch Pull Request semantics: the Loop-Start Branch is the pull request head, the Pull Request Base Branch must differ from the current Loop-Start Branch, and idle or review handoff opens or reuses one Batch Pull Request.
docs/adr/0020-task-pull-request-mode.md:11:Runtime State now records the Pull Request Mode and issue identifier for pull request handoffs, and keeps a list of recorded handoffs while preserving the existing latest `pull_request` field.
docs/adr/0007-stage-goal-handoff.md:1:# Stage Goal Handoff
docs/adr/0007-stage-goal-handoff.md:9:Some Stage Agents benefit from Codex goal tracking, but making `/goal` a global launch mode would change every agent run and blur the boundary between the Stage Goal Context and the normal Agent Prompt.
docs/adr/0007-stage-goal-handoff.md:15:Runtime Settings configure Stage Goal Handoff per stage with `goal.enabled`. Missing `goal` means disabled, and bootstrapped Runtime Settings include `goal.enabled: false` for every example stage.
docs/adr/0007-stage-goal-handoff.md:17:When a matching stage enables Stage Goal Handoff, Symphony prepends `/goal` plus deterministic Stage Goal Context before the normal rendered Agent Prompt. Stage Goal Context includes issue identifier, title, description, issue comments, URL, current project status, labels, priority when present, blocker references when present, attempt, and stage agent name. It does not include issue creation or update timestamps by default.
docs/adr/0007-stage-goal-handoff.md:26:Symphony also verifies that the configured Codex command supports `/goal` from standard input before treating Stage Goal Handoff as supported. A live stdin probe is available with `SYMPHONY_CODEX_GOAL_STDIN_PROBE=1`; otherwise the readiness check accepts the default `codex exec` command shape without consuming a Codex run during ordinary readiness checks.
docs/adr/0007-stage-goal-handoff.md:32:Stage Goal Handoff supplements the Agent Prompt and does not replace stage agent instructions.
docs/adr/0007-stage-goal-handoff.md:34:Stage Goal Handoff does not change retry behavior, completion behavior, status transitions, Stage Commit, Stage Push, auto-merge, or Batch Pull Request behavior.

